"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"Here's what stands out for November 2026, based on search results. I didn't open the full pages, so the details come from snippets.\n\n**Tooling and platforms**\n- **AWS UAEF (Nov 11):** AWS open-sourced the Universal Agent Evaluation Framework under Apache 2.0. It uses adapters to convert traces from LangGraph, LangChain, Strands Agents, Bedrock AgentCore and Langfuse, plus a generic JSON adapter, into one format. It then scores them with [36 built-in metrics across 7 dimensions](https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/uaef-a-framework-agnostic-system-for-closed-loop-evaluation-of-ai-agents). [Tech Times](https://www.techtimes.com/articles/330523/20261112/aws-open-sources-ai-agent-evaluation-framework-that-hardens-its-ai-grader-against-prompt-injection.htm) reports it also hardens the AI grader against prompt injection.\n- **Google Cloud (Nov 14):** Google announced expanded agent observability and evaluation for BigQuery and Looker. [Native BigQuery agent evaluations are in preview](https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/enterprise-ai-agent-observability-with-bigquery-and-looker) via API and a Colab notebook.\n- **Salesforce Agent Evals:** This was announced Oct 27, and [beta is scheduled for November, with general availability in January 2027](https://venturebeat.com/orchestration/salesforce-details-cost-controls-and-kill-switch). It can trigger an agent kill switch when quality drops. [One critic notes](https://salesforcedevops.net/index.php/2026/10/27/salesforce-agent-fabric-evals-2027) that rivals already ship similar features.\n- **OpenAI Evals shutdown:** According to [HatchWorks](https://hatchworks.com/blog/ai-agents/ai-agent-evaluation-frameworks), OpenAI's hosted Evals platform has been read-only since Oct 31. The dashboard and API shut down on **Nov 30**, and Promptfoo is the recommended migration path. [Gamut](https://www.gamut.so/blog/ai-agent-evaluation-guide) says the same.\n\n**Research and benchmarks**\n- **Causal evaluation (Nov 6):** The paper [\"Knowing When to Intervene\"](https://arxiv.org/html/2611.09792v1) tests whether intervening at a given point would change an agent's outcome. It uses τ-bench Retail and ToolSandbox.\n- **LifeVal (Nov 2026):** This benchmark covers personalized agentic consumer tasks. It's listed in [a \"Top 10 Eval Papers of 2026\" thread](https://x.com/omarsar0/status/2122333324895035868), which also highlights SkillsBench and its paired-comparison approach for checking whether a change really helped.\n- **Saturation and validity:** A [Princeton paper on emerging trends](https://sage.cs.princeton.edu/trends/emerging-trends-paper.pdf) from October covers benchmark saturation. SWE-bench Verified is widely treated as compromised. [HoneyHive](https://www.honeyhive.ai/learn/agent-benchmarks) cites OpenAI's February 2026 contamination finding and its recommendation of SWE-bench Pro.\n\n**Upcoming:** [Agent Evaluation Science NYC](https://www.garysguide.com/events/zflvhqr/Agent-Evaluation-Science) is a free one-day symposium on Nov 20.\n\nI haven't verified the OpenAI deprecation against an OpenAI source. Both sources for it are secondary."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1367,"cache_read_input_tokens":1902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8899},"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
